On Jan 26, 11:34=A0am, "hepta...@gmail.com" <hepta...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Is it true that if the player knows of a trap that their pet will be
> aware of a trap, actively avoiding it and the consequences?

     No.  There only two items of information tracked for
each individual trap.  One is whether the hero knows about
it, mainly so that it can be displayed on the map, the
other is whether the hero created it, so that credit or
blame can be assigned if/when a monster is harmed by it.
When monster movement evaluates a location containing a
trap as a candidate destination, it does not take either
of those two bits of information into account.

     Monsters learn about _types_ of traps by surviving
movement onto an instance of the type.  (A few monsters
such as shopkeepers and quest leaders are created with some
or all trap types already learned.)  Once a type has been
learned, all traps of same type are known to that monster,
regardless of whether the hero has discovered them yet.


